=== VERDICT: W12 CONFIRMED, expected NO-GO (reinstall precondition, NOT a defect) ===
STEP 0d FAILs because the INSTALLED /usr/bin/tbard (stale, predates
ADR-041) does not understand --probe-input → exit 2 → 0d FAIL → overall
NO-GO. STEP 2/3 FAILs are the ORACLE-ACTIVE interlock (correct — the
oracle stays lit per HOST SAFETY; we do NOT stop it in a read-only QA
session). The preflight correctly distinguishes:
  - 0a/0b/0c/0e/0f PASS (environment + stale-binary-class checks);
  - 0d FAIL (stale binary lacks the probe — the reinstall trigger);
  - 2/3 FAIL (oracle active — the Stage-3 interlock gate, correct).

This is the reinstall precondition working as designed. After
`makepkg -si` (reinstall /usr/bin/tbard from this branch's tip), 0d will
call the installed probe and PASS (the branch probe ACCEPTed event7 in
Audit B). The strings --probe-input behavioral guard flagged in
self-assessment-10 C6 (preflight 0e checks --service but NOT
--probe-input) is NOT yet implemented; the loud exit-2 failure mode is
the current safety net. ADR proposal: add a 0e-sub-check
`strings /usr/bin/tbard | grep -c -- --probe-input` ≥ 1 (new finding
D-031-1, logged not implemented per FREEZE).